In article <61bmh8$hsu@news.uta.edu> earvin@omega.uta.edu (Earvin C. Lim) writes:

> Hi there,

> We are running DU4.0B, and we want to increase the number of 
> pseudo-terminals. 

> Any insight of how to do that? 

> Thanks in advance!

Easy:

1) cd /dev
2) ./MAKEDEV pty<x>

where <x> is a number indicating a block of 16 pty's.

At installation time, the OS created 32 tty's and 32 pty's using
   ./MAKEDEV pty0
   ./MAKEDEV pty1

If you want to raise it to 64, issue the commands
   ./MAKEDEV pty2
   ./MAKEDEV pty3

And so on for as many as you want.

Keep in mind your license limits though - for example. it would be
pointless to create 128 terminals on a system that only allows 16
simultaneous users.

