Bruce,
      Check out the osf-alpha-managers archive lists. I posted a summary
of what to do there. One way around the crappy disklabel is to find
something close that you ahve on your machine and write that disklabel 
out to an ascii file. Edit the file appropriately and then write
it to the new disk using 

   disklabel -R -r rz** /tmp/jaz.disklabel rzboot bootrz

where rz** is the drive (eg. rz12c) and /tmp/jaz.disklabel is the
ascii file containing the disklabel you have just edited.

Good luck.

