> I'm trying to log to a Digital Unix 3.2 with an X client ( or by telnet)
> with user root but system replies me that root is unauthorized login on
> this terminal.
> 
> I tried to change /etc/securettys without sucess.
> Can someone help me
> 
> Patrick Landureau                               ,,,

The message you recieved refers to bad/no authorisation for the terminal
to login root user. And you guessed correctly, it is in /etc/securettys
file. Since you haven't given us your file, her's an example:

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

:0		# Local X terminal
local:0		# the same

ptys		# This enables telnet and login from dxterm

sun.corp_net:0	# This enable X server from host sun.corp_net to login
root.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

If you have Enhanced security then you must see also /etc/auth/system
directory and it's files ttys and devassign.

That's it. I've tried it, it works.

Nix.



