Well, this isn't a problem with the compiler.  The run-time library does
use DECthreads, but I had thought this was disabled by default.  Your
local Digital support center should know how to submit a problem report
to engineering.

One thing I might suggest, having seen something vaguely similar in the
past, is to increase your process datasize limit.  Try an "unlimit" command
to start with.  If your program is very large, it may exceed the default
datasize for your system.  The amount of physical memory is not directly
relevant.
