milburn@netcom.com writes:

>I am trying to setup automounter so that it will seek through
>different filesystems till it finds the correct user's home dir.
>It works fine on Solaris but I can't seem to make this work
>on Digital UNIX 4.0B.

>auto.home:

>*       oms:/export/home1/& oms:/export/home2/& oms:/export/home3/&
>oms:/export/home4/& oms:/export/home5/& oms:/export/home6/&

Near as I can tell with a cursory look, I don't think our automount
can do that.  It will take a list of servers and figure out the
closest one, but doesn't query the mountd on each to see if the
directory of interest is there.

What most people do for home directories is to make a auto.home NIS
map such that "ypmatch werme auto.home" would report the right
target, e.g. "oms:/export/home5/&".  Less convenient, but faster in
operation since only one server is accessed.
