I see from the output of show device that it is not a Digital CD-ROM
drive, which leads me to suspect that what we have here is either a
firmware problem or kernel driver problem.

One of my customers had an old Digital RRD42 drive which flatly
refused to read things like v3.2C DU distribution media, which was a
bit of a pig, becuase I was trying to do an O/S upgrade at the time.
