Just a thought:
On the unix side I'd try this:

tar -cvf /dev/zipdisk /somedirectory/with/my/files

On the linux side I'd try this:

cd /somedirectory
tar -xvf /dev/zipdisk

And reverse the process for the other direction.

By the way, doing this *will* destroy any filesystem you had on such
a zip disk if any, so please use a blank zip disk that is well and truely 
marked for this purpose.

Regards
Garen

